<title>TAIWAN: Minor leak at Taiwan underground oil pipe.</title>
<headline>Minor leak at Taiwan underground oil pipe.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state monopoly Chinese Petroleum Corp on Thursday reported a leak in a fuel oil pipeline at its northern Taoyuan refinery and said the problem was under control.</p>
<p>&quot;A small fuel oil pipe had some leakage on Thursday during our pumping process,&quot; company official Liao Pai-fung told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;The leak stopped after we closed the pipe.&quot;</p>
<p>Chinese Petroleum expected to replace the pipe soon and resume operations, he said without giving a schedule.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-508-0815)</p>
</text>
